WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.467 --> 00:00:02.834
-Welcome, welcome, welcome
to "The Tonight Show"!

00:00:02.834 --> 00:00:06.968
You're here, you're watching,
I appreciate it.

00:00:06.968 --> 00:00:09.701
Guys, it seems like there's so
much going on right now.

00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:12.501
The supply chain is still
causing problems.

00:00:12.501 --> 00:00:14.601
Paul Rudd was named
"Sexiest Man Alive".

00:00:14.601 --> 00:00:17.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:17.801 --> 00:00:20.300
Adele debuted a new song.

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:22.200
[ Cheers ]

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.434
And Arby's just announced two
French fry flavored vodkas.

00:00:25.434 --> 00:00:28.267
[ Laughter ]
There's just a lot to go over.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:29.767
So let's just jump in and cover
it all at once.

00:00:29.767 --> 00:00:32.067
It's time for a "News Smash."
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:32.067 --> 00:00:36.000
♪♪

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.000
First up, the supply chain.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:40.234
President Biden just met with
several companies

00:00:40.234 --> 00:00:42.667
like Walmart, Target, and FedEx
to discuss solutions

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:44.400
and it's not looking great.

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.200
But, you know
who is looking great?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.567
Paul Rudd.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:47.567 --> 00:00:50.934
He was named "People's"
Sexiest Man Alive. Good for him.

00:00:50.934 --> 00:00:53.434
He's universally beloved.
He makes us all laugh.

00:00:53.434 --> 00:00:55.567
But if you prefer someone
who's universally beloved

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.400
and makes us all cry,
there's always Adele.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
She just debuted a new song

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.334
in an Amazon holiday commercial,
and it's fantastic.

00:01:03.334 --> 00:01:05.734
The song is called "Hold On,"
and it's all about

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:07.033
not giving up.

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:10.000
But if you want to give up,
why not try Arby's new

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.234
French fry vodka.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.968
They're releasing two bottles,
and apparently,

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:17.000
they have the same
"flavor profile"

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.334
as their curly
and crinkle-cut fries.

00:01:19.334 --> 00:01:20.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:20.701 --> 00:01:22.767
I don't understand
how that would even work.

00:01:22.767 --> 00:01:25.501
Speaking of things I don't
understand, the supply chain.

00:01:25.501 --> 00:01:28.467
[ Laughter ]
Shipping, trucking, inflation,

00:01:28.467 --> 00:01:30.000
all of it has people really
stressed out.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.567
But it's going to be okay.

00:01:31.567 --> 00:01:34.400
Just take a deep breath,
pour yourself some wine

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:35.501
and listen to Adele.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.501 --> 00:01:37.634
The new album drops next week.

00:01:37.634 --> 00:01:39.934
Her first album was "19,"
loved that.

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:43.100
[ Cheers and applause ]
Then "21," loved that.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:46.167
[ Cheers and applause ]
Then "25," and now "30."

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:48.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
We're really -- we've really

00:01:48.133 --> 00:01:49.801
seen her grow up over the years.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.133
You know who hasn't grown up?

00:01:51.133 --> 00:01:52.367
Paul Rudd.
I mean, look at the guy.

00:01:52.367 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:53.434 --> 00:01:56.200
He -- he only gets better
with age.

00:01:56.200 --> 00:01:58.067
You know what doesn't
get better with age?

00:01:58.067 --> 00:02:00.234
Arby's vodka.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:00.234 --> 00:02:01.934
I -- I just don't get it.

00:02:01.934 --> 00:02:04.267
I mean, from the vodka itself
to the label,

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:06.467
all the way to the bottleneck.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:06.467 --> 00:02:08.133
Everything's
completely backed up.

00:02:08.133 --> 00:02:09.934
So it'll affect prices.

00:02:09.934 --> 00:02:11.033
And if you order
anything online,

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.367
be prepared to "hold on."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:16.300
In conclusion, what a guy.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:17.601
Time to cry,

00:02:17.601 --> 00:02:19.100
low supply,

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:20.534
just why?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:20.534 --> 00:02:22.033
This has been a "News Smash"!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:28.200
♪♪

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:29.934
Thank you.

00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:31.167
Hey, here's some COVID news.

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.734
Apparently,
the U.S. government

00:02:32.734 --> 00:02:35.067
helped Moderna
develop their vaccine.

00:02:35.067 --> 00:02:37.033
And now they're in
a patent fight

00:02:37.033 --> 00:02:39.501
over who deserves credit for it.

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:41.300
Yeah, even crazier, they're
going to settle it on a --

00:02:41.300 --> 00:02:44.834
with a rap battle on "VERZUZ."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:44.834 --> 00:02:46.167
Meanwhile,
there's also a battle

00:02:46.167 --> 00:02:48.300
over the Johnson &amp; Johnson
patent because

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:49.567
nobody wants to
take credit for it.

00:02:49.567 --> 00:02:51.934
[ Laughter ]
No, it was the other Johnson.

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:54.100
[ Laughter ]
Some business news.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:57.100
YouTube just announced that it
is hiding dislike counts

00:02:57.100 --> 00:02:59.567
on all videos.
That's right.

00:02:59.567 --> 00:03:01.400
Now instead of clicking
thumbs down,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.367
people will just write "dislike"
in the comments.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.934
[ Laughter ]
"Not for me."

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.834
[ Laughter ]
Yep, no more dislikes.

00:03:08.834 --> 00:03:11.501
Instead, YouTube will provide
the user's home address

00:03:11.501 --> 00:03:12.767
so you can just tell them
in person

00:03:12.767 --> 00:03:15.234
how much you hated their video.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.234 --> 00:03:16.634
Yeah, dislikes are annoying.

00:03:16.634 --> 00:03:18.634
They're right up there with
people who comment "first!"

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:20.734
It's like,
"Oh, it's just stop."

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:22.033
Well, the holidays
are coming up,

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.968
and I read that 'cause of the
tight labor market,

00:03:23.968 --> 00:03:26.868
there's actually a shortage
of mall Santas.

00:03:26.868 --> 00:03:28.567
[ Audience "aws" ]

00:03:28.567 --> 00:03:30.801
Yeah, malls are desperate
to find Santas.

00:03:30.801 --> 00:03:32.934
Today, in fact, Macy's put out a
bowl of whiskey

00:03:32.934 --> 00:03:35.601
outside the store like they were
trying to lure a stray cat.

00:03:35.601 --> 00:03:39.868
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:41.067
-Putting a bowl of whiskey
out there.

00:03:41.067 --> 00:03:43.400
-For Santas.
Yeah, it's hard to recruit

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:44.868
for the job,
because you can't just

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.834
walk up to people like, "Hey,
you're built like Santa Claus.

00:03:46.834 --> 00:03:50.000
Do you want to --"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.501
That's right.
No mall Santas.

00:03:51.501 --> 00:03:52.834
Instead,
it'll just be an elf saying,

00:03:52.834 --> 00:03:54.467
"Whatever you want, it's on
Amazon. Merry Christmas."

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.667 --> 00:03:57.200
Hey, get this,
The Hallmark Channel

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:00.501
is holding a baking contest
and the grand prize is

00:04:00.501 --> 00:04:06.000
a walk-on role in a Hallmark
original movie or $5,000.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.434
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:08.868
Even the director of the
Hallmark movie was like,

00:04:08.868 --> 00:04:12.067
"Take the money!"
[ Laughter ]

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:14.501
Seriously, for 5 grand, you can
shoot your own hallmark movie.

00:04:14.501 --> 00:04:16.567
-Yeah.

00:04:16.567 --> 00:04:19.434
-Hey, here's good news, the
North American Meat Institute

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.901
said it will reach
Paris Agreement

00:04:20.901 --> 00:04:23.133
emission targets by 2030.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:24.534
When I heard,
my first thought was,

00:04:24.534 --> 00:04:26.367
"There's a North American
Meat Institute?"

00:04:26.367 --> 00:04:28.367
[ Laughter ]
Sounds less like a real

00:04:28.367 --> 00:04:30.033
organization and more like
something you'd read

00:04:30.033 --> 00:04:31.901
on the shirt of a dude
at CrossFit.

00:04:31.901 --> 00:04:35.501
[ Laughter ]

00:04:35.501 --> 00:04:36.767
It's a long walk
but it's worth it.

00:04:36.767 --> 00:04:38.400
I like that joke. Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:40.033
And finally,
according to new research,

00:04:40.033 --> 00:04:42.067
it's perfect --
the perfect time to go to bed

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:46.968
for your heart's health is
between 10:00 and 11:00 P.M.

00:04:46.968 --> 00:04:49.167
Probably explains why NBC ran a
promo today that said,

00:04:49.167 --> 00:04:51.000
"Forget your heart and catch an
all-new episode of

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:52.133
'The Tonight Show.'"
[ Cheers and applause ]

